<title>USA: Marriott sees Renaissance deal diluting EPS.</title>
<headline>Marriott sees Renaissance deal diluting EPS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marriott International Inc said it expects its proposed $1 billion acquisition of Renaissance Hotel Group NV to dilute earnings per share through 1998.</p>
<p>In response to a question during a media conference call detailing the transaction, Marriott chief financial officer Michael Stein said 1997 earnings would be trimmed by about $0.10 to $0.14 per share, assuming a first quarter deal closing.</p>
<p>Earnings in 1998 would suffer a similar reduction because of the acqusition, he said.</p>
</text>
